# Twin Call Tracker - optional configuration
#
# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in only what you need. Keep the real .env out
# of version control: it is already covered by .gitignore.
#
# NOTHING IN HERE IS A USER PASSWORD. The values below identify the OAuth
# *application*, not a person. Each member of staff still signs in to their own
# account, and their tokens are stored encrypted on their own machine.
#
# The application runs perfectly well with this file absent:
#   * Monday.com works with a personal API token pasted into the app.
#   * Google Sheets works with a client_secrets.json file placed in the
#     application data folder (see the README section "Google setup").


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Sheets  (required for the Google connection)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two APIs must be enabled in the Google Cloud project: Google Sheets API, and
# Google Drive API for the folder browser. Without the Drive API everything still
# works except the Browse Google Drive button, and the app says so.
#
# Preferred: download client_secrets.json from the Google Cloud console and put
# it in the application data folder. The About screen shows the exact path,
# normally:  C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Local\TwinCallTracker\client_secrets.json
#
# Point at a different location if you keep it elsewhere, for example on a
# read-only network share that everyone in the office can reach:
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRETS_FILE=\\fileserver\apps\TwinCallTracker\client_secrets.json

# Alternative to the file: supply the desktop OAuth client directly.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=000000000000-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Monday.com  (optional - only for browser sign-in instead of an API token)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave these unset and the app will ask each user for a personal API token,
# which is what Monday.com recommends for an internal tool. Set them only if you
# have registered a Monday OAuth app and want staff to sign in through a browser.
# MONDAY_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# MONDAY_CLIENT_SECRET=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application update check  (optional - see requirement 23)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An internal URL returning JSON: {"version": "1.1.0", "url": "...", "notes": "..."}
# Left unset, the About screen simply reports that no update server is configured.
# It never contacts anything on its own.
# TCT_UPDATE_URL=https://intranet.example.com/apps/mondaygooglesync/latest.json


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diagnostics
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Write debug-level detail to the log file. Credentials are redacted either way.
# TCT_DEBUG=1

# Move settings, the sync database and logs somewhere else. Useful for testing
# against a scratch configuration without disturbing the real one.
# TCT_DATA_DIR=C:\Temp\mgs-test
